   <indicator ascending="1" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">3. The percentage of atolls with approved disaster plans including climate adaptation measures.</narrative>
    </title>
    <baseline iso-date="2024-04-14" value="0 percent (FY24)" year="2024">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN"></narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2024-04-14"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2027-09-14"></period-end>
     <target value="25 percent (FY27)">
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">While disaster plans for all atolls are approved and are in the process of being socialized with the DRM focal points, they are yet to incorporate climate adaptation measures per the DRM Act. For example, coastal adaptation measures especially to address coastal inundation and erosion remain a critical gap. The NDMO remains committed to incorporating climate adaptation in the disaster plans although funding for technical assistance to support the updates is needed. Under the Pacific Resilience Program II &#xe2;&#x20ac;&#x201c; RMI (PREPII-RMI, financed by the WB), a technical adviser is working on the necessary institutional reforms to better integrate DRM and climate adaptation to inform the updated disaster plans. This includes developing terms of references for a new Resilience Committee that is awaiting government approval. NDMO will continue seeking funding opportunities to support the updating of disaster management plans, including from WB. The target is on track to be achieved by the end of FY27.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual value="0 percent"></actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Intermediate Results Indicator</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="1" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">6. The percentage of new national government buildings with a building permit issued.</narrative>
    </title>
    <baseline iso-date="2024-04-14" value="0 percent (FY24)" year="2024">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN"></narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2024-04-14"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2027-09-14"></period-end>
     <target value="100 percent (FY27)">
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Bill was revised in late 2024 to incorporate some minor editorial changes and to incorporate provisions for setting fees for building permit applications. The Cabinet approved the revised Bill in early Feb 2025 and will undergo three public readings before approval by Nitijela. MPWIU has established a new Building Safety and Regulations division to implement the Bill and administer the National Building Code (NBC). WB technical assistance is providing support to the BSR on a package of policies (including for fees), standard operating procedures, templates and forms for the implementation and enforcement of the NBC, in line with the National Building Bill. The International Code Council, financed under URP, carried out technical training in early Feb 2025 on NBC enforcement. A resilient multifunctional government facility, incorporating the NDMO, humanitarian warehouse and MoFBPS functions, received a building permit in April 2025. The target is on track to be achieved by end FY27</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual value="100 percent"></actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
